<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Darius's Scythian campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">513 BCE</span> · Also known as Scythian campaign</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Darius's Scythian campaign was a military expedition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> in 513 BCE. The Persian army crossed the Bosporus and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, but the nomadic Scythians avoided pitched battle and withdrew, forcing Darius to retreat. The campaign illustrated the limits of Persian military power against mobile steppe peoples.</p></div>
